---
layout: base.njk
splash: true
permalink: /index.html
title: "HELM Core"
description: "Telemetry display script for Space Engineers Programmable Blocks."
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
<section class="splash-hero text-center pt-4 sm:pt-8">
  <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-black font-mono"><span class="text-primary">HELM</span> Core</h1>
  <p class="mt-4 text-base sm:text-lg text-base-content/70 max-w-2xl mx-auto" style="font-family: 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif;">
    Draws telemetry on Space Engineers LCDs and cockpit screens from a Programmable Block. You describe screens in a text configuration; there is nothing to mod.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3">
    <a href="/docs/getting-started/" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm font-mono">Get started</a>
    <a href="/docs/" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm font-mono">Documentation</a>
    <a href="{{ site.repoUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm font-mono">Repository</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mt-10" aria-label="Example displays">
  {% set first = presets.splash[0].split(":") %}
  <div class="hv hv-medium not-prose" data-helm-viz data-controls="minimal"
       data-layout="{{ first[0] }}" data-profile="{{ first[1] }}"
       data-cycle="{{ presets.splash | join(',') }}" data-cycle-seconds="9">
    <figure class="preset-shot preset-shot-empty"><figcaption>Example displays need the generated frame files: run <code>bun run frames</code> in <code>docs/</code>.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p class="mt-3 text-center text-xs text-base-content/50 font-mono">
    Frames come from the script's own renderer; text widths are approximate. {{ presets.count }} layouts are included, see the <a class="link link-hover" href="/docs/presets-gallery/">gallery</a>.
  </p>
</section>
